Subject: [PATCH 04290/11362] [outer-loop] S3 BOUNDED on generation (no lift)
 -- pending a guidance-exercised no-op check

S3 (.444 A1, exp4821) wired E as goal_energy into live plan_in_model() and tested generation
lift on 24 headroom games vs a matched lambda=0 control: winners-newly-entering-pool delta 0.0,
CI [0,0], zero new levels, positive_control_passed, live_path_reachable, e_guided_attempts=4/game.
Well-controlled BOUNDED null -- BUT the artifact does NOT show lambda=1 materially changed
generation vs lambda=0, so the 0.0 could be a silent no-op (the S2 degeneracy lesson). Strengthened
the .444 B1 audit (exp4825) to verify s3_guidance_exercised (lambda=1 produced different proposals
than lambda=0); the S3 verdict is only trustworthy if that passes. Do NOT conclude the program yet.

IF genuine, the staged energy program (S0'->S1->S2-v3->S3) reaches its honest END: the structural
energy is a real OFFLINE discriminator with NO live value at selection OR generation; S4 is moot.
A clean negative answer to 'does extend-with-energy work on ARC': offline yes, live no.

